@host = http://localhost:5105
@token = COLE_AQUI_O_TOKEN_RETORNADO_POR_/api/auth/login

### 1) Registrar usuário (login/senha) — grava o hash em Data/users.csv
POST {{host}}/api/auth/registrar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "SenhaForte@123"
}

### 2) Login — valida login/senha e devolve o token JWT (Bearer)
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "SenhaForte@123"
}

### 3) Analisar currículos (protegido: exige Authorization: Bearer <token>)
POST {{host}}/api/analisar
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary

------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="descricaoVaga"

Desenvolvedor .NET com experiência em C# e Python
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="curriculos"; filename="teste-a.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

@teste-a.txt
------WebKitFormBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="curriculos"; filename="teste-b.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

@teste-b.txt
------WebKitFormBoundary--

### 4) (alternativa) mesma chamada via curl:
# curl.exe -X POST http://localhost:5105/api/analisar ^
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer {{token}}" ^
#   -F "descricaoVaga=Desenvolvedor .NET com C# e Python" ^
#   -F "curriculos=@teste-a.txt" ^
#   -F "curriculos=@teste-b.txt"